00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.125
he has a long list of complaints

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:26.559
about the former president.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.660
A big spender, he says,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.895
not tough enough at the border.

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.597
He says friend of Fauci

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.632
to damage to win the White House again.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:33.366
There's more.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:33.900
As Governor,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.336
DeSantis looks to use his first days

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.537
as an official candidate

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.071
to reset

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:38.972
both his campaign

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.640
and to reset the broader contours

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.841
of a Republican race.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:42.575
The right now

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.744
is being run on Trump's turf.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.812
It is a tight rope

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:48.248
no Republican has managed to walk before,

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:49.749
take on Trump

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:50.450
without earning

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.485
the ire of his loyal base.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.421
This is how Governor Santos right here

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.189
hopes to keep his balance with Trump,

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.291
like promises to purge the deep state

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:00.460
and to look even at giving clean slates

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:01.861
to insurrectionists.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:05.532
Do you think the January six defendants

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.267
deserve to have their cases

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.868
examined by a Republican

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.770
president on day one?

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.872
I will have folks that will get together

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.741
and look at all these cases

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:17.343
who people are victims of weaponization

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.845
or political targeting,

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.080
and we will be aggressive

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.248
in issuing parties.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.616
Let's get straight to Miami.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:24.951
CNN's Steve Van Tornoe is there.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.486
Steve, it is an interesting

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:29.189
and a risky strategy

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.291
That's right, John.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.826
I've been covering government instances

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:34.494
for the better part of the last decade.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.595
I have heard him speak

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.097
